{#
  The body of a received message, the one way every screen shows it.

  Four screens used to render it four ways — a card on /courrier, a
  monospace <pre> in a dialog on the camps screen, a monospace <pre>
  always expanded on a booking, a <details> on a stay — and a reader who
  had learned one found the next unfamiliar. This partial is the body;
  the screen around it decides only whether it opens folded.

  The HTML was sanitised and stripped of remote images when the message
  was STORED (§7.9), never at render time, so no screen has to remember.
  The text body keeps its line breaks and wraps like prose: monospace is
  for code, and a farmer's reply is not code.

  Parameters:
    message   -- the Modules\InboundMail\Api\InboundMessage
    folded    -- true to render behind a native <details> whose summary is
                 « Lire le message »; false (default) to show it outright
#}
{% set has_text = message.bodyHtml is not empty or message.bodyText|trim is not empty %}
{% if folded|default(false) and has_text %}
    <details class="inbound-message">
        <summary class="btn btn-link btn-sm p-0 inbound-message__toggle">
            <i class="bi bi-envelope-open" aria-hidden="true"></i> Lire le message
        </summary>
        <div class="inbound-message__body mt-2">
            {% include '@inbound_mail/partials/message_text.html.twig' with { message: message } only %}
        </div>
    </details>
{% else %}
    <div class="inbound-message__body">
        {% include '@inbound_mail/partials/message_text.html.twig' with { message: message } only %}
    </div>
{% endif %}
